  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Adding to this https://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/no-way-for-non-trusted-users-to-know-how-broken-their-avatar-looks-to-others allowing creators access to VRChat's safety system is important for model creators and shader developers because VRChat's fallback shader system can be a bit buggy. For instance this is a friend of mine that uses Poiyomi, their fallback shader was set to Toon/Opaque/DoubleSided and with safety settings enabled the model doesn't look right on top of other issues in regards to inverted normals for their clothing. even when the normals were fixed the shadow ramp was a bit too aggressive on the map we were on. So please expose those options in the SDK to allow us creators to test these issues.",
